      "The stock looks undervalued relative to historical norms, but the discount is logically tied to the fact that the forced CRM migration introduces uncharacteristic volatility into a historically predictable revenue model. Analysts rightly questioned the full-year revenue guidance raise to $3,635 million to $3,645 million, representing a roughly $45 million bump from the high end of previous guidance, which some viewed as conservative following a strong Q1 beat. Management attributed this caution to complex enterprise product integrations and clarified that AI monetization will remain immaterial this fiscal year."
